fferings born from compliance). 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 = paradigm preserving.\n\nUnified framework is just tool for compliance logging. Introduces new elements but treats compliance as logging practice. So slightly paradigm stretching? Might be 2. It introduces library but relationship unchanged. Probably 2.\n\nOriginality: degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious... 4 = not expressed before AND ingenious. 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. 2 = interesting. 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nUnified compliance logging framework is common practice. Common, mundane. So 1.\n\nWe need output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? Return rating. Might be simple list.\n\nI'll produce:\n\nid: P1522\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\n...\n\nLet's craft one sentence evidence each.\n\nAcceptability evidence: The proposal uses standard software library and logging to meet legal requirements, which aligns with regulatory expectations and does not offend norms. Score 4.\n\nImplementability evidence: Building a common API and integrating it into all training and deployment pipelines requires coordinated engineering effort across diverse projects, which is reasonably feasible but not trivial. Score 3.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: Automatic capture of timestamps, dataset versions and input-output pairs directly satisfies Article 12's mandatory automatic logging and traceability requirements. Score 4.\n\nApplicability evidence: The framework addresses the lab's need to meet the EU AI Act logging mandate for high-risk AI systems. Score 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: It introduces new tools and processes for compliance logging but keeps compliance separate from R&D rather than changing the relationship between research and obligations. Score 2.\n\nOriginality evidence: A standardized logging library for regulatory compliance is a common, mundane industry practice. Score 1.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
