nusual interesting shows some imagination 2 = interesting 1 = common mundane boring\n\nUnified middleware for logging is fairly common idea in industry; not rare. Maybe interesting but common. I'd say 1 = common, mundane, boring? Or 2 = interesting. The concept of wrapper library for compliance logs is common. Probably 1? Might be 2 interesting. Let's think: experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give this response. Yes, unified logging middleware is a standard expected response. So common, mundane. Score 1.\n\neffectiveness: degree to which idea will solve problem. 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability... 3 = reasonable and will contribute... 2 = unreasonable or unlikely... 1 = solves unrelated problem\n\nWill automatic capture of logs meet Article 12? It captures inputs outputs timestamps piping into vault. Does it capture required events? Article 12 requires logging capabilities enable recording of events relevant for identifying risks, post-market monitoring, monitoring operation. For point 1(a) Annex III systems need period of use, reference database, input data for match, identification of natural persons. Middleware intercepts inputs outputs timestamps - seems plausible. It removes need for researchers to write custom code. So it will solve problem. Reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? Might be 4.\n\napplicability: degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem. 4 = solves identified problem directly related... do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. This is direct. Score 4.\n\nacceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms. This is common. Score 4.\n\nimplementability: degree can be easily implemented. 4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes. Developing shared internal library that intercepts... That is some changes, reasonably feasible measures? Might be significant change expensive difficult but not totally impossible. Engineering team develop shared library - requires engineering effort, integration across projects. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Not easy low cost. Could be 3.\n\nSo final:\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It introduces a shared logging wrapper tool but still treats compliance as separate logging practice rather than changing R&D-compliance relationship.\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Unified middleware for automatic compliance logging is a common, widely expected engineering response for regulated AI labs.\noriginality: 1\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Automatic capture of inputs, outputs and timestamps via a wrapper would provide the required logs to meet Article 12 traceability mandates.\neffectiveness: 4\n\napplicability_evidence: The middleware directly addresses how to meet the logging mandate for high-risk AI R&D projects.\napplicability: 4\n\nacceptability_evidence: Centralized logging to a secure regulatory vault is a standard, legally compliant practice that violates no norms.\nacceptability: 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building and integrating a shared interception library across diverse research projects requires moderate engineering effort and coordination.\nimplementability: 3\n\nReturn rating echoing id.\n\nNeed format? Probably JSON-like. Provide each.\n\nLet's output structured.\n\n",
