htly paradigm stretching? It minimizes admin burden allowing prioritize innovation. Still compliance as separate. I think 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\n4 reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 reasonable and will contribute to solution\n2 unreasonable...\nProblem is how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. This addresses documentation burden, not directly logging mandate? Recital 71 requires technical documentation kept up to date and logs. Automated pipeline updates dossier from logs, which helps meet record-keeping and documentation. Will solve problem of administrative burden but does it ensure automatic recording of events logs over lifetime? It parses log metadata and updates dossier during versioning. Might contribute but not guarantee logging capabilities per Article 12(2)(a)-(c). Effectiveness maybe 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (partial). Not full solve logging mandate.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 solves identified problem directly related\n3 solves implied problem related\nIdea applies directly to meeting documentation requirement from Recital 71. Stated problem: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. This addresses record-keeping/documentation. So applicability 4? It solves identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem). Yes.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 common strategies violate no norms\nThis is standard compliance automation. Acceptable. 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 some changes, reasonably feasible\nAutomated CI/CD pipeline parsing logs and updating dossier: requires engineering effort, integration with model versioning, but feasible. Might be some changes, reasonably feasible. Not trivial low cost? Could be 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible.\n\nThus ratings:\noriginality_evidence sentence then originality 2?\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence then 2\neffectiveness_evidence then 3\napplicability_evidence then 4\nacceptability_evidence then 4\nimplementability_evidence then 3\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence each.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly.\n\nFormat: maybe JSON? Instruction says for each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\" integer. Probably output lines.\n\nProvide id P2319 then entries.\n\nLet's produce clear listing.\n\n",
