dea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related\nProblem: must decide how to respond: meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources.\nProposal directly addresses meeting logging mandate by verifying logs capture events. So applicability 4.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution\nWill sandbox guarantee technical viability and regulatory compliance? It helps verify but doesn't implement logging itself. It contributes. Might be 3? The proposal says guarantees technical viability and regulatory compliance before deployment. If you could do it, would it solve main problem? The main problem is meet logging mandate and adapt R&D. Sandbox verifies logs work, but does not create logs. It contributes to solution. Could be 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4):\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving\n\nSandbox introduces new element tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. That's slightly paradigm stretching? Might be 2. It doesn't change relationship between R&D and compliance fundamentally, just adds testing. So 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious imaginative surprising\n3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane boring\n\nCompliance verification sandbox is fairly common idea - test environment for compliance. Might be interesting but not rare. Could be 2 = interesting. Or