        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument... Apply published anchored levels exactly...\n\nWe need rating for proposal P2548.\n\nProposal: Unified Telemetry Wrapper for High-Risk Prototypes. Standardized software library providing consistent event logging interfaces across all lab projects. Ensures essential metadata captured by default. Python decorator/middleware wraps model inference calls to automatically record inputs and execution times to secure database. Prevents developers manual implement. Maintains prototyping speed while ensuring technical viability for regulatory compliance.\n\nWe need six subscales:\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nProblem: AI R&D lab subject to regulation must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources...\n\nProposal is unified telemetry wrapper to automatically record inputs and execution times. That directly addresses Article 12 record-keeping: automatic recording of events logs over lifetime, recording period of each use start/end, input data etc.\n\nDoes it solve identified problem directly related? It does X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. The stated problem is how to meet logging mandate. This wrapper provides logging. So applicability = 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Evidence sentence.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? It captures timestamps and input references. Article 12 requires logs of events relevant for identifying risk situations, post-market monitoring etc, and for point 1(a) Annex III systems need period of use, reference database, input data for match, identification of natural persons involved in verification. Wrapper records inputs